<br>

> **💬 Quick Reflection:** Does this graphic align with your experience as an educator?

AI is unlikely to replace teachers. Instead, it works best as a teaching assistant that helps reduce workload and support daily tasks. By handling routine or time-consuming work, AI can give educators more time for instruction, coaching, and relationship-building. When used thoughtfully, AI may also help reduce teacher burnout and support schools facing staffing challenges.

In Module 3, Transforming Teaching with AI, you’ll explore how educators can use AI to save time on preparation, grading, feedback, and administrative tasks.
